# {{ service_slug }}

Thin service generated by the Rust Knative + FluxCD platform. It is built on the
shared `crates/service-core` crate, so configuration, error types, application
state, tracing/metrics, HTTP middleware, health endpoints, Kafka plumbing, and
startup/shutdown are not duplicated here.

## What this crate owns

- `src/routes.rs` - router, rate limiting, OpenAPI, and shared health endpoints
- `src/handlers/` - demo handlers (`/api/v1/hello`, plus the CloudEvents echo when
  the Knative KafkaSource sink is enabled)
- `config/` - default and per-environment configuration
- `migrations/` - this service's migrations (PostgreSQL only)

## Endpoints

| Path | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `GET /health/live` | Liveness probe |
| `GET /health/ready` | Readiness probe (Redis, plus optional PostgreSQL/Kafka) |
| `GET /metrics` | Prometheus metrics |
| `GET /api/v1/hello` | Demo greeting (`?name=...`) |
{%- if kafka_source %}
| `POST /` | CloudEvents echo consumed from the Knative KafkaSource |
{%- endif %}
| `GET /swagger-ui` | OpenAPI UI |

## Configuration

Configuration is layered by `service-core`: defaults, then
`config/development.toml` or `config/production.toml`, then `APP__*`
environment variables (for example `APP__REDIS__URL`).
{%- if include_postgres %}

This service owns the `{{ db_name }}` database on the shared CloudNativePG
cluster. Its migrations run at startup against that database.
{%- endif %}
{%- if kafka_publish %}

Kafka publishing is enabled; events use the `{{ kafka_topic }}` topic.
{%- endif %}

## Deploy unit

This service owns its complete deploy subtree under
`services/{{ service_slug }}/deploy/`:

- `base/` - one Flux `HelmRelease` for `{{ service_slug }}`, rendering the
  project's local `deploy/chart` (pinned `ksvc` chart 1.2.1). The sourceRef is
  the platform `GitRepository` (`{{ project_slug }}` in `flux-system`).
{%- if include_postgres %}
- `base/database.yaml` - a CloudNativePG `Database` CR for `{{ db_name }}` on
  the existing `{{ pg_cluster }}` cluster. This service never creates a second
  Cluster, Pooler, ObjectStore, backup, or operator.
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_s3 %}
- S3 wiring reuses the project-level `{{ project_slug }}-app-data`
  Secret/ConfigMap. This service never declares `objectBuckets`.
{%- endif %}
- `overlays/{dev,staging,prod}` - per-environment namespace, scaling/replicas,
  resources, and environment values.
{%- if enable_image_updates %}
- `flux/` - per-service `ImageRepository`/`ImagePolicy` objects in
  `flux-system`; the project's shared `ImageUpdateAutomation` remains the only
  automation object.
{%- endif %}

### Workload

{% if workload_deployment %}
This service renders a plain Kubernetes `Deployment` plus a core `Service` and
a `PodDisruptionBudget` (chart 1.2.1). It emits no Knative Service, no
`autoscaling.knative.dev` annotations, and no HPA. Exposure follows
`services.app.service.type` (`ClusterIP` by default; `NodePort` and
`LoadBalancer` are supported by the chart) - there is no Knative URL/ingress.
{% else %}
This service renders a Knative `Service` with the chart's scaling settings.
{%- if kafka_source %}
It also renders a Knative `KafkaSource` for `{{ kafka_topic }}` and an
auto-generated dead-letter Service `{{ service_slug }}-{{ kafka_topic }}-dlq`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if enable_flagger %}
Flagger canary promotion is enabled with the environment's Prometheus metric
gates and the chart's k6 load test disabled.
{%- endif %}
{% endif %}

### Chart 1.2.1 limitations

- No HorizontalPodAutoscaler is rendered for Deployment workloads.
- Flagger canaries target Knative Services only; the chart fails closed for a
  Deployment.
- KafkaSource sinks must reference a Knative Service, so Deployment services can
  publish to Kafka but cannot consume through a KafkaSource.
- The 1.2.1 `pingsources` feature is not used by this template.

## Run locally

```bash
cargo run -p {{ crate_name }}
